      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: For me personally it's an annoyance but not a big deal. However there are many scenarios where this won't be so simple. For Example: \n- SDK2 avatars, \n- people who have had their avatar commissioned by an artist (which is often specifically because they lack the kind of technical knowledge to do this sort of thing),\n- Public avatars from authors who are no longer active on the platform.\n- Anyone who has lost the source files of their avatar.\nI'd say that unless the performance hit is worse than how dynamic bones are currently then it's probably worth it.\nOf course, the checkbox can still be off by default in the SDK, but for auto conversions the compatibility seems more important. \nI imagine the ideal solution would be some way of detecting if at least the root bone is animated and or humanoid during conversions, and setting based on that, but I don't know if/how that could be done.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
